WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
Speaker 1: The Pennsylvania Senate race is one of&nbsp;
the most interesting elections this midterm cycle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.000
as it presents Democrats with an opportunity to&nbsp;
pick up a seat in the upper chamber and add to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.760
their majority. Democratic nominee John Fetterman&nbsp;
is up against Republican Mehmet Oz, and this race&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.080
was considered a toss up just a couple of months&nbsp;
ago. But it's now looking like Fetterman really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:26.160
is pulling away. The FiveThirtyEight average&nbsp;
of polling has Fetterman up by 11 points 49%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:32.080
to 38%. And part of this can be expected because&nbsp;
Pennsylvania, still, after all, is a blue state.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:38.080
Yes, they did vote for Trump in 2016. They've put&nbsp;
people in power like Rick Santorum and Pat Toomey.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:43.680
But this is still blue territory, we can say. But&nbsp;
another part of the reason is that Mehmet Oz, Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:49.200
Oz, he really just seems to be a lot weaker of a&nbsp;
candidate than many of us even expected. He's been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.400
painted successfully as a carpetbagger because&nbsp;
he's from New Jersey. He's been painted as an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:59.680
elitist, which is also true because he has a net&nbsp;
worth of about $100 million with ten houses. More&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.560
on that later. On today's bonus show, we actually&nbsp;
talked earlier in the week on the bonus show about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.440
his crew to take video, which was filmed back&nbsp;
in April. But it's going viral now. And John&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.520
Fetterman was mocking him for it because he didn't&nbsp;
know the name of the grocery store that he was in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.960
He didn't know how buying vegetables works. And&nbsp;
oftentimes the price that's listed is the price&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.920
per pound versus the price per vegetable. So&nbsp;
the Fetterman campaign was having a field day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.720
trolling him for that. Well, the OSI team is&nbsp;
realizing that they have to make up some ground&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:35.040
and they've decided to go on the offense. They did&nbsp;
so by releasing an attack ad on John Fetterman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.400
and I don't think it's going to work out too&nbsp;
well for them. Let's take a look at the ad.&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.280
Speaker 3: Now that John Fetterman claims to be&nbsp;
recovering. Let's pull back his hoodie and examine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:52.000
what's in his head. Looks like he has some screws.&nbsp;
What's this? That one wants to release one third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:59.920
of all prisoners. That's crazy. To spend more tax&nbsp;
dollars, everything will cost more. That's nuts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:09.200
Slow energy production. Gas prices will&nbsp;
skyrocket. That's ridiculous. Socialized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:17.600
medicine. Get these crazy ideas, and now it&nbsp;
makes a mess. Well, Bob, let her close it up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.040
John Fetterman is crazier than you think.
Speaker 1: All right, so in the ad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.920
they attack John Fetterman for wearing a hoodie,&nbsp;
which actually can be argued is an asset for him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.400
The fact that he just dresses like the average&nbsp;
Pennsylvania dude, he's not trying to be anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.200
that he's not. He's not wearing a suit and&nbsp;
tie just for the show. He likes wearing his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.800
basketball shorts and his sweatshirts. So&nbsp;
I don't know if that's going to be all that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:46.080
effective for the odd campaign. Then there's&nbsp;
this bong that pops out of veteran's head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:51.200
and I couldn't find out whether Fetterman himself&nbsp;
uses cannabis, but he is one of the most pro weed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:56.240
politicians in America. He supported it long&nbsp;
before it was politically popular to do so.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:02.480
And the latest poll that I could find was that 58%&nbsp;
of Pennsylvanians support legalizing marijuana. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:07.680
I don't see how that is much of an attack either.&nbsp;
Then there's this bit about releasing a third of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.880
prisoners while we do have the world's highest&nbsp;
prison population. And if you're talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:17.360
releasing people who are nonviolent, people who&nbsp;
are maybe drug offenders, that sort of thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.920
yeah, they should be let out of prison. That's&nbsp;
totally cool. By the way, I thought Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.960
were all of a sudden more amenable to this idea of&nbsp;
prison and criminal justice reform, because they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:31.360
think that the January 6th rioters are spending&nbsp;
too much time behind bars. Maybe they forgot about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.160
that over at the Oz campaign. Then there's the&nbsp;
thing about slowing energy production. Clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.720
that's over the course of many years and decades,&nbsp;
though, to move in the direction of renewable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:46.720
power that will ultimately save people money, by&nbsp;
the way, and save the planet in the long term.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:52.320
And then they put up the phrase free health care&nbsp;
being held up on a sign by AOC, which they should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.480
have known that they shouldn't have used the&nbsp;
term free health care, universal health care.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.720
It would have been much better if they used&nbsp;
the term government takeover of health care,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:04.480
they said in the ad, socialized medicine, but they&nbsp;
should have put that on the sign as well, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.760
that's the type of phrase that polls a lot better&nbsp;
for Republicans. And then out pops Bernie Sanders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:14.960
who is apparently the one who's really controlling&nbsp;
John Fetterman. If you vote for John Fetterman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:19.280
you're actually getting Bernie Sanders. I think&nbsp;
this is another blunder, too, because, yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:24.960
Bernie wasn't popular enough to win the Democratic&nbsp;
primary, for example, either in 2016 or 2020. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.760
he is quite popular as a politician. People think&nbsp;
that he's principled and he's especially popular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.480
in the Northeast, in states like Vermont, where he&nbsp;
represents. And, you know, Pennsylvania is pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:39.600
close by, too, so I'd imagine he's pretty popular&nbsp;
there. So even though I'm no Republican, I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.800
that I could have done a much better job at making&nbsp;
this attack ad on John Fetterman, because this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:50.960
just looks absolutely cartoonish. It's a terrible&nbsp;
presentation, very over-the-top. And I think the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:56.240
team could have done a lot better. Let's hope that&nbsp;
Fetterman is able to grow or at least maintain his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:01.360
lead will be able to land Donald Trump another&nbsp;
loss if Fetterman picks up the victory here. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.960
you know what Trump will do? If Mehmet Oz ends&nbsp;
up losing, he'll just distance himself from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:09.840
Oz and say, Well, Austin, it really run all&nbsp;
that close to me. And that's why he lost. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:14.640
nonetheless, it will be a glorious victory if&nbsp;
we're able to pick up this seat in Pennsylvania.

